{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"docker.io/victoriametrics/victoria-metrics","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:05:26.745Z","source":{"name":"Docker Hub","api":"https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/victoriametrics/victoria-metrics/","page":"https://hub.docker.com/r/victoriametrics/victoria-metrics"},"readme":"<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://victoriametrics.com/icons/apple-touch-icon.webp\" width=\"150\" alt=\"VictoriaMetrics logo\"/>\n</p>\n<h1 align=\"center\">VictoriaMetrics</h1>\n\n[![Join our SLACK Community](https://img.shields.io/badge/Join%20our%20SLACK%20Community-621773?style=for-the-badge&logo=slack&logoColor=white)](https://inviter.co/victoriametrics/)\n[![File a Bug on GitHub](https://img.shields.io/badge/File%20a%20Bug%20on%20GitHub-E94600?style=for-the-badge&logo=github&logoColor=white)](https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics/issues)\n[![Source Code](https://img.shields.io/badge/Source%20Code-323232?style=for-the-badge&logo=github&logoColor=white)](https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics)\n</p>\n\n---\nWhat is victoria-metrics?\n-------------------------\n\nvictoria-metrics is the single-node version of VictoriaMetrics, a fast, cost-effective, and scalable time series database (TSDB) and monitoring solution. It combines all the necessary components for ingestion, storage, and querying into a single, easy-to-deploy binary, making it perfect for small to medium-sized setups or for getting started quickly.\n\nHow to Use This Image\n---------------------\n\nRun a single-node VictoriaMetrics instance:\n\n`docker  run  -d  --name  victoriametrics  -p  8428:8428  victoriametrics/victoria-metrics:latest`\n\nCommon Scenarios:\n\nPersisting Data: To store data on the host machine, mount a volume to the container.\n\n```bash\ndocker run -d --name victoriametrics -p 8428:8428 \\\n  -v /path/to/vmdata:/victoria-metrics-data \\\n  victoriametrics/victoria-metrics:latest \\\n  -storageDataPath=/victoria-metrics-data\n```\nConfiguration\n-------------\n\n-   `-storageDataPath`: The path to the directory where time series data is stored. Default: victoria-metrics-data.\n\n-   `-retentionPeriod`: Specifies how long to keep the data. For example, 3m for 3 months or 1y for one year. Default: 1m (1 month).\n\n-   `-httpListenAddr`: The TCP address to listen on for HTTP requests. Default: :8428.\n\nAdvanced Usage\n-------------\n\nWhile the flags above cover common use cases, VictoriaMetrics is highly configurable. You can view all available configuration flags, their descriptions, and default values by passing the `--help` flag to the container.\n\n`docker  run  --rm  victoriametrics/victoria-metrics:latest  --help`\n\nFor comprehensive details on configuration and tuning, please refer to the[  official documentation](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/).\n\nBenchmarking VictoriaMetrics\n-------------\n\nVictoriaMetrics is built for performance and resource efficiency. We encourage you to compare it against other time series databases like TimescaleDB, InfluxDB, Thanos, Mimir, M3, and Cortex on your own workloads.\n\nWhen comparing, pay close attention to RAM usage, CPU usage, and on-disk storage size. and feel free to share your results with the community!\n\nWhere to Get Help\n-----------------\n [![Join our SLACK Community](https://img.shields.io/badge/Join%20our%20SLACK%20Community-621773?style=for-the-badge&logo=slack&logoColor=white)](https://inviter.co/victoriametrics/)\n\n[![File a Bug on GitHub](https://img.shields.io/badge/File%20a%20Bug%20on%20GitHub-E94600?style=for-the-badge&logo=github&logoColor=white)](https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics/issues)\n\n[![Source Code](https://img.shields.io/badge/Source%20Code-323232?style=for-the-badge&logo=github&logoColor=white)](https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics)\n\nSource Code\n-----------\n\nThe source code for victoria-metrics is available on GitHub: <https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaMetrics>","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"victoriametrics","url":"https://hub.docker.com/u/victoriametrics","official":false,"verified":false},"registered":"2019-06-07T08:43:59.529614Z","updated":"2026-09-14T07:28:39.696585Z","categories":["Databases & storage","Monitoring & observability"],"keywords":[],"license":null,"links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":100114491,"stars":68},"mediaTypes":["application/vnd.docker.container.image.v1+json","application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json"],"contentTypes":["image"],"storage":59621913454,"tags":[{"name":"latest","digest":"sha256:86ca5fdb6d87d56ba047b044039019ba2bd9042b36e35f6ea34e437b6c825cef","pushed":"2026-09-14T07:28:38.33752Z","size":18912752,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/arm64","linux/386","linux/arm/v7","unknown/unknown"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"v1.152.0-enterprise-fips","digest":"sha256:50fd6baca3ef97bbec1d95472bffa89d3fec27627bcd7c9c7745d545e5307b43","pushed":"2026-09-14T07:24:07.677304Z","size":15366632,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/arm64","linux/386","linux/arm/v7"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":"active"},{"name":"v1.152.0-enterprise-scratch","digest":"sha256:0b0a51f6976b223a668c2e55ac8e57af5f3fd85545d819d725f8a62e38dccfc9","pushed":"2026-09-14T07:23:58.828854Z","size":15452578,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/arm64","linux/386","linux/arm/v7","unknown/unknown"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"v1.152.0-enterprise","digest":"sha256:f9a7b6517625e0734cb1b69beea02f7351fc6cea8ebd9939027d290cd8887d0b","pushed":"2026-09-14T07:23:50.994183Z","size":19298981,"platforms":["linux/amd64","linux/ppc64le","linux/arm64","linux/386","linux/arm/v7","unknown/unknown"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.oci.image.index.v1+json","status":"active"},{"name":"v1.152.0-scratch","